The TypeScript adaptation keeps the filter stateless and frame by frame. It
refuses, instead of approximating, every layout native would remix implicitly
(anything but stereo), timeline enable, runtime commands, option expressions
and constants, non-finite input samples, and NaN output without clipping. It
adds no FFmpeg runtime code. The original source and full notices remain in
the pinned upstream submodule.
